# Lychee ignore — patterns excluded from the link-check workflow.
#
# Each pattern is a regex. Add a comment above any new entry explaining
# why it's excluded and when it can be re-enabled.
#
# Lesson: A brand-new page's own canonical URL does not exist in production
# until it deploys, so link-check on that PR can flag it; add a temporary
# entry with a removal note and delete it in the next PR.

# Placeholder Snowflake account URL used in the Snowflake/Matillion lab
# examples — readers substitute their own account locator.
^https://myaccount\.snowflakecomputing\.com

# Oracle sites (GoldenGate blog + LiveLabs/OTN forum) return 403 to
# automated link-checkers via bot protection; the links are valid in a
# browser. Referenced from the GoldenGate lab's resources.
^https://blogs\.oracle\.com/
^https://apexapps\.oracle\.com/

# Fivetran community forum intermittently refuses automated requests.
^https://community\.fivetran\.com/

# LinkedIn rate-limits and blocks automated link-checkers (HTTP 429 / 999),
# but the author profile link on module pages and in the footer is valid in
# a browser. Referenced from src/_data/author.mjs (sameAs, advisoryUrl).
^https://www\.linkedin\.com/

# The maintainer's GitHub profile page (the byline/footer author link, from
# src/_data/author.mjs; ~46 occurrences). A cold request to it is slow to
# render (~10 s from an ordinary connection); from shared CI runner IPs
# GitHub's gateway gives up first and answers [504] Gateway Timeout. lychee
# does not retry a 5xx (checked against lychee 0.24.2, the newest release:
# one request to a server answering 504, no retry, with --max-retries 3), so
# retry settings cannot fix it, and accepting 5xx would hide real outages on
# every other link. Anchored to this exact URL, so every other
# github.com/sandgraal/... link (repo, blob, discussions) is still checked.
# Same precedent as the LinkedIn entry above: a link we control that is
# valid in a browser.
^https://github\.com/sandgraal/?$
